id: pm-vcs-p7sign
title: Sign changes with ed25519 and enforce trusted keys on publication
description: "Sign change ids using ed25519, configure a trusted-key file and validate signatures at the publication boundary. Preserve signature validity across rewrites that retain change identity."
type: Feature
pm_format_version: 2
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-18T03:01:46.220Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-20T14:54:05.007Z"
author: codex-agent
estimated_minutes: 480
acceptance_criteria: "verify --signatures checks trusted ed25519 signatures; configured serve and push refuse unsigned or untrusted changes before ref publication; malformed, revoked and tampered signatures fail closed; signing keys never enter history."
parent: pm-vcs-phase7
dependencies[1]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
  pm-vcs-p7objects,blocked_by,"2026-10-18T03:01:55.791Z",codex-agent,"cli:update:dep",detected
comments[22]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-20T07:04:49.950Z",codex-agent,"Design: explicit sign command avoids implicit key access during commit/rewrite. Ed25519 signs a versioned domain-separated canonical payload binding stable change id, tree, author, message and sorted pm item links; parents and committer are excluded so ancestry-only rewrites preserve validity. Content-changing rewrites remove the attestation and require explicit signing. Receiver policy binds SHA-256 SPKI fingerprints to author email identities and has effective-time revocations. Administrative trust/revoke operations share the object-store write lease with push; policy is reloaded under ref locks immediately before the complete batch publishes. Both HTTP and filesystem publication use that boundary. Private key files must be external to the repository and errors never include key bytes."
  "2026-10-20T07:16:46.490Z",codex-agent,"Implementation and focused adversarial suite are in place. Receiver checks only requested publication closure, including all ancestors, not unrelated uploaded objects; forged series publication also enforces policy. Effective-time revocations are evaluated after crypto at the transaction boundary. Focused suite passed 14/14 before the additional rebase scenario; actual rebase scenario passed 1/1. Full unchanged-threshold coverage is running. verify --signatures reports all rows in a nonzero error on failure because the existing pm host cannot return a structured report together with a nonzero exit (documented pm-cli #826 limitation). No dependency pins changed."
  "2026-10-20T07:22:38.119Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof in isolated source copies: replacing only assertTrustedChanges with its pre-feature no-enforcement behavior made all 4 selected filesystem push, resumable publish, HTTP and forge refusal tests fail (0 pass, 4 fail). Replacing only retainedAttestation with no retention made both selected rewrite tests fail (0/2); unconditional retention also made both fail (0/2), catching stale content signatures. Unmodified focused source passed 15/15, plus linked-instance CLI coverage passed 2/2. New signature-policy and cryptographic modules and signing commands each measured 100% statements, branches, functions and lines in focused coverage. Final release gates remain pending. The linked-test timeout was raised to 600 seconds after the default 120-second run timed out on the shared host; no coverage threshold changed."
  "2026-10-20T07:25:14.135Z",codex-agent,"Review candidate: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/pull/134 (draft until full release gates finish). The pinned pm linked runner passed the complete focused suite 16/16 with zero failures, cancellations, skips or todos; 2000/2000 native changes verified in 16760.378 ms including object-integrity and history reads under shared-host load. Test-result tracking is disabled by existing tracker policy, so this comment preserves the result. Strict pm health exited 0 and validate returned ok with existing repository advisories; no history was repaired. Typecheck, lint, zero-duplication and docstring checks passed. The PR contains the design, threat table, before/after and behavioral revert proof. The final unchanged-threshold npm and Bun gates will be recorded on that linked PR. Implementation is ready for orchestrator review; retain in_progress and do not close or merge."
  "2026-10-20T07:27:29.297Z",codex-agent,"Final publication timing review identified a scheduled-revocation boundary worth tightening: a key can reach its effective revocation time while other receiver preflights run after cryptographic verification. Retain the crypto/trust result under the writer lock and recheck effective revocations immediately after FileId lease checks, before the first ref write. Adding an actual transport regression with real lease checks delayed across a scheduled effective time. This also preserves lease-expiry checking after expensive cryptography."
  "2026-10-20T07:30:05.606Z",codex-agent,"Final timing regression passes (1/1); reverting only the final moveRefs revocation recheck makes it fail (0/1, missing rejection). It advances the receiver clock after the real FileId lease preflight to make the scheduled-time boundary deterministic, while leaving crypto, policy, objects, refs and transport real. Native Bun Ed25519 signing/verification smoke also passed 1/1. The full linked suite was rerun after this change; final release-gate evidence is attached through PR #134."
  "2026-10-20T07:30:23.212Z",codex-agent,"Updated linked-suite receipt: 17 tests, 17 pass, 0 fail/cancelled/skipped/todo; pm test runner exited 0. The same 2000-change full native verification benchmark measured 4770.950 ms on this run. Timing varies with shared-host load; no performance guarantee or coverage threshold adjustment is inferred. Full release gates on the final committed candidate remain pending on PR #134."
  "2026-10-20T07:32:15.160Z",codex-agent,"Final benchmark now invokes the actual vcs verify --signatures command handler through the real extension loader, including receiver policy-file reads, native object verification, reachable-history reads and the full 2000-row result; all 2000 signatures were valid in 6473.737 ms on the focused run. CI CodeQL flagged the intentionally rejected 1024-bit RSA fixtures; these negative-test keys are strengthened to 2048 bits so algorithm-refusal coverage remains without weak-key examples. Production signing remains Ed25519 only. Scheduled revocation rechecks are also documented after FileId lease preflights."
  "2026-10-20T07:53:16.788Z",codex-agent,"CI Node 22 and Node 26 measured every production file at 100% statements, branches, functions and lines, including all signing code. Each ran 1728 tests: 1727 passed and exactly one failed because the existing raw-coverage guard still expected 70 production files instead of 73. Updating only that explicit inventory count for the three new modules; coverage includes, thresholds and ignore-directive prohibitions remain unchanged. Both local full gates are being restarted on the resulting committed head. CodeQL and Windows launcher checks pass."
  "2026-10-20T07:54:05.467Z",codex-agent,"Inventory correction verified with node --test test/raw-coverage.test.ts: 3/3 pass, zero fail/cancelled/skipped/todo. The inventory now explicitly counts all 73 measured production files; the no-suppression rule and per-file 100% coverage gates are intact. Releasing the implementation claim for final exact-head release checks and orchestrator review; item remains in_progress."
  "2026-10-20T10:16:13.153Z",codex-agent,"Review round 1: verified all six unresolved PR 134 findings against remote head 58263f9. Complete thread/comment pagination; latest CodeRabbit review has no Outside diff range section. Branch contains current main. Fix receiver-only configuration filtering on advertisement and adoption, atomic config replacement, caller-attributed signing rewrites, pre-write reachability and fingerprint validation, and signed-author tamper tests. Audit the full diff for matching defect classes and record behavioral revert proofs."
  "2026-10-20T10:19:08.481Z",codex-agent,"All six findings are valid. Receiver-only trustedKeysFile is filtered by an allowlist on FileTransport advertisement, HTTP advertisement parsing and clone adoption; fetch does not adopt config. All config writes now reuse the native atomic private JSON writer (exclusive sibling, file fsync, rename, supported directory fsync). Sign uses caller Signature for descendants and preserves the target committer; unreachable commits are refused before planning writes. Unknown revocation fingerprints are refused before persistence. Added independent tampering for every author field. Tests use real native repositories in plain temporary directories without Git. Full-diff review also caught HTTP normalization retaining the marker, now covered with a legacy HTTP server regression. No other matching instance found in the PR diff."
  "2026-10-20T10:21:11.991Z",codex-agent,"Review round 1 behavioral revert proofs: isolated copies of current native TypeScript source, one function behavior reverted at a time, real stores and real transports; no source mutation in the package worktree. Each selected regression: exit 1, 0 pass, 1 fail; fixed focused source: 35/35 pass, zero fail/cancel/skip/todo. PM-linked execution: 34/34 pass before the legacy HTTP parser test was added; evidence recording remains tracking_disabled, so results are recorded here. Additional unborn-HEAD orphan refusal: 1/1 pass. advertise (engine/transport.ts): node --test --test-name-pattern=file advertisement and clone test/signatures.test.ts => 0/1 pass, 1 fail. clone-adoption (engine/sync.ts): node --test --test-name-pattern=clone adoption filters test/signatures.test.ts => 0/1 pass, 1 fail. http-adoption (engine/http-transport.ts): node --test --test-name-pattern=HTTP parsing discards test/signatures.test.ts => 0/1 pass, 1 fail. committer (engine/repo.ts): node --test --test-name-pattern=sign attributes descendant test/signatures.test.ts => 0/1 pass, 1 fail. reachability (engine/repo.ts): node --test --test-name-pattern=sign rejects unreachable test/signatures.test.ts => 0/1 pass, 1 fail. unknown-revocation (engine/signature-policy.ts): node --test --test-name-pattern=unknown and malformed revocations test/signatures.test.ts => 0/1 pass, 1 fail. author-name (engine/signatures.ts): node --test --test-name-pattern=canonical domain/version test/signatures.test.ts => 0/1 pass, 1 fail. author-timestamp (engine/signatures.ts): node --test --test-name-pattern=canonical domain/version test/signatures.test.ts => 0/1 pass, 1 fail. author-timezone (engine/signatures.ts): node --test --test-name-pattern=canonical domain/version test/signatures.test.ts => 0/1 pass, 1 fail. atomic-config (engine/config.ts): node --test --test-name-pattern=config replacement leaves test/config.test.ts => 0/1 pass, 1 fail. Thread mapping: PRRT_kwDOToJT7M6uSSRO = receiver policy filtered on advertisement, clone adoption and HTTP parse; PRRT_kwDOToJT7M6uSSRU = caller committer for descendants; PRRT_kwDOToJT7M6uSSRZ = reachability before writes; PRRT_kwDOToJT7M6uSSRn = atomic config writer; PRRT_kwDOToJT7M6uSSRu = reject unknown revocation fingerprints; PRRT_kwDOToJT7M6uSSR0 = every signed author field tampered independently. All six valid; no thread replies or resolutions. Typecheck/test compile, lint, zero-percent duplication and 73-file/410-declaration docstring checks pass. Full npm and Bun release gates are next, unchanged 100 percent thresholds."
  "2026-10-20T10:28:18.575Z",codex-agent,Merged main 78a5aad (PR 132 toolchain update and its self-host acceptance changes) after it advanced during preliminary gates. Only generated selfhost.bundle conflicted; regenerating from combined staged source. Reinstalled the merged lockfile. Preliminary npm lint caught require-atomic-updates in the legacy HTTP cleanup; fixed with a synchronous restore helper. Lint now passes and the legacy HTTP parser regression passes 1/1. Preliminary Bun gate was stopped; no preliminary full-gate pass is claimed. The newly inherited pinned pm 2026.10.15 refuses all tracker writes with project_runtime_item_format_incompatible because the package peer range admitted pre-2026.10.10 runtimes. Aligned only the peer minimum and README to the guard floor 2026.10.10; pinned SDK/tool versions remain exactly those from main. No existing history was rewritten. Strict local tracker health separately fails extension_host_pm_cli_version_skew for ambient pm-github 2026.10.20 versus the pinned host; stale-item and historic provenance findings are advisories. No merge receipts were pending. Treat this as separate evidence from release checks.
  "2026-10-20T10:28:23.521Z",codex-agent,"Reproducible shell equivalents for revert proofs (the pattern is one argv value): advertise: node --test '--test-name-pattern=file advertisement and clone' test/signatures.test.ts; clone-adoption: node --test '--test-name-pattern=clone adoption filters' test/signatures.test.ts; http-adoption: node --test '--test-name-pattern=HTTP parsing discards' test/signatures.test.ts; committer: node --test '--test-name-pattern=sign attributes descendant' test/signatures.test.ts; reachability: node --test '--test-name-pattern=sign rejects unreachable' test/signatures.test.ts; unknown-revocation: node --test '--test-name-pattern=unknown and malformed revocations' test/signatures.test.ts; author-name: node --test '--test-name-pattern=canonical domain/version' test/signatures.test.ts; author-timestamp: node --test '--test-name-pattern=canonical domain/version' test/signatures.test.ts; author-timezone: node --test '--test-name-pattern=canonical domain/version' test/signatures.test.ts; atomic-config: node --test '--test-name-pattern=config replacement leaves' test/config.test.ts. Each selected test: exit 1, 0 pass and 1 fail only with its named production behavior reverted. Fixed focused suite: 35/35 pass."
  "2026-10-20T12:04:53.850Z",codex-agent,"Review round 1 acceptance at immutable c837cefe5021739bd5928fba9dadac8ed794bb8d: npm run release:check and bun run release:check both exited 0. Each ran 1740 tests: 1740 pass, 0 fail/cancelled/skipped/todo. Both measure all 73 production TypeScript files individually at 100 percent statements, branches, functions and lines; scope, thresholds and suppression rules are unchanged. Also passed native TOON, actual installed CLI/stat-cache strace, committed self-host archive equality, production dependency audit (zero vulnerabilities), Git identity audit, package dry run, changelog equality and release verifiers. The Bun script ran in an independent clone of the same head; both used disposable homes and disabled Git global/system configuration. Native Bun Ed25519/atomic-config/advertisement/revocation smoke in a plain directory without Git passed 1/1. Clean-home strict tracker health and separate validation pass; ambient host extension skew remains separate. The original PR item history is preserved byte-for-byte as a prefix. Inspected all ten revert logs: nine assertion failures plus the legacy clone bad_signature_policy failure, with no syntax or module-loading failures. Fixed focused suite passed 35/35. Linked evidence persistence is disabled; these receipts are recorded here."
  "2026-10-20T12:04:55.054Z",codex-agent,"Finalization: align manifest pm_min_version to the peer minimum 2026.10.10 so runtime admission agrees with the pinned host format guard. No pinned SDK/tool versions changed beyond those inherited from main. Regenerate the self-host bundle with this admission metadata and the acceptance receipts, then run both full release checks on that immutable final head before pushing. All six thread fixes and the extra HTTP normalization fix are complete; threads remain open for reviewer verification. Releasing the implementation claim for final immutable acceptance; item remains in_progress for the orchestrator."
  "2026-10-20T12:25:50.814Z",codex-agent,"Final-head verification at 221728a caught one failure in each run: manifest-vocabulary.test.ts deliberately asserts the original public extension API floor 2026.8.1 independently of the development toolchain. Raising manifest pm_min_version was unnecessary and has been reverted to the original value; the test is unchanged. The peer minimum 2026.10.10 remains necessary for the pinned host to write guarded project tracker formats. Both final-head gates were stopped after identifying the same metadata assertion; no full-gate pass is claimed for 221728a. No TypeScript source or test differs from the fully passing c837cef head. Regenerate and rerun both complete release gates on the corrected immutable head before pushing."
  "2026-10-20T14:12:35.024Z",codex-agent,"Review round 2: fetched all review threads with complete comment pagination. Two unresolved threads: PRRT_kwDOToJT7M6uWB1u (detached HEAD descendant replay) and PRRT_kwDOToJT7M6uWB1z (conflicting published minimum host versions). Latest CodeRabbit review has no Outside diff range section. Remote head fc71fd0 contains current main. Verify and fix both with behavioral revert proofs, audit all descendant replay callers and host admission metadata, then regenerate the native self-host bundle and run both full release gates at unchanged thresholds. Real native fixtures remain plain directories without Git."
  "2026-10-20T14:15:11.966Z",codex-agent,"Both round 2 findings confirmed. replayWithDescendants now receives HEAD explicitly, walks detached history as well as branches/tags, and serves both ordinary rewrites and planResolution without duplicate tip-selection logic. Real CLI signing regressions cover a HEAD-only ancestor and a shared ancestor, assert reachable valid signatures, preserved child content/authorship/change identity, named-ref moves, detached HEAD and single-operation undo. Full-diff audit found describe, rebase, squash and split share the same defect; four native regressions cover them. Runtime floor is now consistently 2026.10.10 in manifest, peer metadata and README; pinned SDK/tool dependencies unchanged. The installed pinned SDK project-runtime guard explicitly rejects dependency declarations below 2026.10.10 for guarded tracker formats, so lowering the peer minimum is unsafe. Updated manifest vocabulary assertion and added actual compatibility admission tests rejecting 2026.8.1 and 2026.10.9 and admitting 2026.10.10. Typecheck/test compile, lint, zero-duplication and docstrings pass."
  "2026-10-20T14:16:09.101Z",codex-agent,"Round 2 behavioral revert proofs completed in an isolated source copy with real native repositories, unchanged tests and no worktree source mutation. Reverting only detached-tip selection inside replayWithDescendants: node --test \"--test-name-pattern=sign replays detached HEAD\" test/signatures.test.ts => exit 1, 0/2 pass, 2 assertion failures (live HEAD unchanged); node --test \"--test-name-pattern=replays descendants carried only\" test/rewrite.test.ts => exit 1, 0/4 pass, 4 assertion failures. Restoring only manifest pm_min_version to 2026.8.1: node --test \"--test-name-pattern=published host requirements\" test/manifest-vocabulary.test.ts => exit 1, 0/1 pass, 1 assertion failure. No syntax or module-load errors. Fixed focused commands: 8/8 pass. Pinned pm linked execution of node --test test/signatures.test.ts test/rewrite.test.ts test/manifest-vocabulary.test.ts: exit 0, 77/77 pass, zero fail/cancel/skip/todo; evidence persistence is disabled by existing policy (tracking_disabled), so this comment preserves the receipt. Entire PR diff audited for descendant-tip parity, receiver-only configuration boundaries, atomic policy/config writes, signed-field preservation and host admission contracts; no additional instance found beyond the four shared rewrite callers fixed here. Dist is ignored and untracked; production build is regenerated by gates. Both unresolved threads are valid; no replies or resolutions made."
  "2026-10-20T14:54:03.621Z",codex-agent,"Round 2 acceptance at immutable b8bfb96682deeb7ccf35a23a9682bb917a5d0c43: npm run release:check and bun run release:check both exited 0. Each ran 1747 tests: 1747 pass, 0 fail/cancelled/skipped/todo. Both measured all 73 production TypeScript files individually at 100 percent statements, branches, functions and lines. Thresholds, measurement scope and suppression rules unchanged. Native TOON, actual installed CLI/stat-cache, independent committed self-host archive verification, production dependency audit, identity audit, package dry run, changelog equality and release verifiers passed. Both used disposable homes and disabled Git global/system configuration, with independent checkouts/build/coverage outputs. No gate timeouts or retries were needed. Native Bun detached-signing smoke in a plain directory without Git: 1/1 pass, including reachable valid parent signature, HEAD movement, preserved branch and undo. Clean-home strict pm health and separate validate both exited 0 with existing advisories. Existing history remains an exact byte prefix. Final same-class documentation audit also found the Requirements sentence omitting the host-provided SDK despite runtime imports in engine/ignore.ts and engine/record-format.ts; clarify that sentence. Final receipt commit changes only tracker evidence, that wording and the native archive; run both complete release gates again on that final immutable head. PRRT_kwDOToJT7M6uWB1u and PRRT_kwDOToJT7M6uWB1z are fixed; no thread replies or resolutions. Item remains in_progress for orchestrator verification."
